<title>NETHERLANDS: Philips posts modest rise in semiconductor sales.</title>
<headline>Philips posts modest rise in semiconductor sales.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics said on Thursday its semiconductors activities had managed to buck the decline in the chip market, posting moderate nominal sales growth of six percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Since we do not sell memory products, we were able to show positive though moderate nominal growth of six percent (in dollar terms one percent),&quot; Arthur van der Poel, chairman of Philips semiconductors, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
